Some time ago I declared that I would bring forth a patch that would
make it so that all monster gaze attacks follow the same mechanics
(because is there any logical explanation for why they shouldn't?) and
also make it so that applying mirrors to Yeenoghu and Baalzebub
reflects their gaze attack, which currently doesn't happen.

So:

http://www.greyfire.org/~l/mirrorfix.diff

Here are the new rules for the Evil Eye:

* All gaze attacks require both participants to be unblind (Nothing new
here.)
* All gaze attacks can be reflected back onto the monster (or, if you
have a gaze attack, yourself) by applying a mirror.
* _No_ gaze attacks can be reflected by the Reflection attribute.
Firstly, this is because wearing a reflective item should _not_ prevent
the monster from making eye contact. Secondly, some reflection-giving
items (amulet of reflection, Longbow of Diana) don't even have a
mirror-like surface, and as such are designed purely for the magical
deflection of ray attacks.
* But, you can now apply a polished silver shield and use it like a
mirror. Thus you can still fulfill the old legend of Perseus reflecting
Medusa's etc...
* Yeenoghu's confusion attack is now a separate gaze attack rather than
one of his weapon attacks.
* If a monster gazes at another monster, they will both be affected by
each other's gaze attacks.

